course: dictionary
lesson: 14683
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words change their meaning depending on the sentence around them. Pressing is one of these words. The context tells you which meaning is right. «She kept pressing the button at the crossing until the green light came on.» Here pressing means pushing firmly on something, because you press a button with your finger.
explain: «The flowers were pressing between two heavy books to dry flat.» Here pressing means making something flat by pushing on it. Pressing is the -ing form of the verb press, so when you see press, presses, pressed or pressing, look at the words around it.
explain: «We have a pressing problem: the bridge is closed and the school trip leaves at nine.» Here pressing is an adjective. It means urgent, something that needs doing now. Ask yourself: is someone pushing something, or is something urgent? The clues will show you.
fact: Pressing is the -ing form of the verb press: press, presses, pressed, pressing.
fact: Pressing can mean pushing firmly on something, as in «pressing the button» at a crossing.
fact: Pressing can mean making something flat, as in «pressing flowers» between heavy books.
fact: As an adjective, «a pressing matter» is something urgent that needs doing now.
fact: Pressing can also mean asking again and again, as in «pressing him for an answer».
exercise: «She kept pressing the button at the crossing.» What does pressing mean here? | Running away fast | Singing loudly | *Pushing firmly on something | Painting a picture
exercise: «We have a pressing problem that needs solving today.» What does pressing mean here? | Heavy and difficult to lift | *Urgent, needing to be done now | Quiet and hidden | Flat and smooth
exercise: Leo says, «I am pressing my shirt before school.» What is he doing to his shirt? | Washing it in the sea | Hiding it under his bed | Tearing it | *Ironing it flat and smooth
test: «Dad kept pressing him for an answer until he told the truth.» What does pressing mean here? | Pushing a button | Hugging tightly | Singing softly | *Asking again and again
test: Which word is the -ing form of press? | presses | *pressing | pressed | pressure
exam: Mum said, «Keep pressing on, the finish line is near.» What does pressing on mean? | Pressing flowers | *Continuing, carrying on | Stopping for a rest | Going to sleep
